            <ArticleTitle>Right coronary artery aneurysm with associated arteriovenous fistula.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>192-4</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe a 47-year-old man who had a right coronary artery aneurysm measuring 78 x 69 mm which communicated to the right ventricle. The lesion was asymptomatic. The myocardial blood supply was highly dependent on the left coronary artery.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
